        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">The core processes of ACT</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">The goal of ACT is not to suppress symptoms but to build psychological flexibility: the capacity to move towards what you value even while difficult feelings are present. If you are looking for an approach that examines the content of thoughts directly, see our <a href="/en/services/cbt-therapy.html" class="text-primary hover:underline">CBT page</a>.</p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Acceptance</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Making room for difficult emotions rather than suppressing them returns the energy the struggle consumes.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Cognitive Defusion</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Learning to see a thought as something the mind produces rather than as absolute truth.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">The Present Moment</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Mindfulness practice brings attention back from the pull of past and future to the here and now.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Values and Committed Action</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">We clarify what matters to you and plan small, sustainable steps in that direction.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
