        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">When does ACT come to the fore?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">ACT is most useful when the struggle with a feeling has itself become exhausting. Rather than trying to remove anxiety, the work is about moving towards what matters to you while anxiety is present. These are the areas we most often use ACT for.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-ink-muted">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>When the energy spent fighting anxiety has become tiring in itself</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span><a href="/en/blog/burnout-syndrome.html" class="text-primary underline hover:no-underline">Burnout</a> and a sense of drifting from your values</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Difficulty alongside chronic pain or an ongoing health condition</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Being caught in "if I could stop feeling this, I could live"</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

